# 604, 644 soft start
(F,"If the cell cannot give it, the remedy is a series resistor or a soft start by pulse train on the pin MOTOR; neither is designed here.","If the cell cannot give it, the remedy was a series resistor or a soft start by pulse train on the pin MOTOR; neither is designed here (2026-11-13: the soft start is NOT a ready fallback and is not built in software step 6: the pin MOTOR drives the enable pin of U11, and stepping that line would charge U11's output capacitor several times; the circuit simulation tests a stepped enable first; the fixed measures are C84 at 4.7 uF and the cell requirement of 1.9 ohm at 3.45 V with a 235 mA pulse, lead-decisions.md row 'motor soft start').",LD+"'motor soft start (correction of \"sim finding 4\")' 2026-11-13 04:09"),
(F,"(2) a soft start (a series resistor, or a pulse train on the pin MOTOR) that keeps the motor's start under about 60 mA;","(2) a soft start (a series resistor, or a pulse train on the pin MOTOR) that keeps the motor's start under about 60 mA (2026-11-13: not a ready fallback, see line 604; lead-decisions.md row 'motor soft start');",LD+"'motor soft start'"),
